     {"question": "Can users access storage without Data Explorer access?", "answer": "Yes. Storage permissions are separate from table permissions. A user can browse and manage files without having access to any database tables."},
     {"question": "How do I link a file to a database record?", "answer": "Configure the column as a storage data type (Image, File, Video, Audio) in table settings. When editing records, users can then pick files from storage or upload new ones directly."},
     {"question": "What happens to files when I delete a database record?", "answer": "Storage files are not automatically deleted. The file remains in storage even if the record referencing it is deleted. Implement database triggers or scheduled cleanup jobs if you want automatic file deletion."}
